    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Johnny has 7 different colored marbles in his bag. In how many ways can he choose 3 different marbles from his bag?  \nTo determine how many ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles from a bag of 7, we use the \"choose\" notation (denoted \"C\" or \"nCr\") which represents the number of ways to choose r items from a set of n items without regard to order. The formula is given by:\n\\[ C(n, r) = \\frac{n!}{r! \\cdot (n-r)!} \\]\n\nHere, \\(n = 7\\) (total marbles) and \\(r = 3\\) (marbles to choose).\n\nLet's calculate the required value step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\ntotal_marbles = 7\nchosen_marbles = 3\n\n# Calculate the number of ways to choose r items from n items\nways_to_choose = math.comb(total_marbles, chosen_marbles)\nprint(ways_to_choose)\n```\n```output\n35\n```\nThe number of ways Johnny can choose 3 different marbles from his bag of 7 is \\(\\boxed{35}\\).",
