      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles, we can use the concept of combinations. \nWe have 7 different colored marbles to choose from, so we will calculate the number of possible ways to choose 3 marbles from the total of 7.\nThe formula for combinations is C(n, r) = n! / (r!(n-r)!), where n is the total number of objects to choose from, r is the number of objects to choose, and ! denotes factorial.\nIn this case, n = 7 (total marbles) and r = 3 (marbles to choose).\nC(7, 3) = 7! / (3!(7-3)!)\n= 7! / (3!4!)\n= (7*6*5) / (3*2*1)\n= 35 ways\nSo, there are 35 different ways Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag.",
