    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We want to find the number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles from 7 different colored marbles. This is a combination problem.\nWe can use the formula for combinations to solve this problem.\n\nC(n, k) = n! / (k! * (n - k)!)\n\nwhere C(n, k) represents the number of combinations of n items taken k at a time.\n\nSo, the number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles from 7 different colored marbles is C(7, 3).\n\nC(7, 3) = 7! / (3! * (7 - 3)!)\n\nC(7, 3) = 7! / (3! * 4!)\n\nC(7, 3) = 7 * 6 * 5 / (3 * 2 * 1)\n\nC(7, 3) = 35\n\nTherefore, Johnny can choose 3 marbles from his bag in 35 different ways.",
